    "adapt": "Spring Pond lies 62 m from the barn b64, which is only the anchor (the kit keeps the barn's own yaw). The pond is a lake shape whose surface is 15.0 m, 2.5 m above its bed at the centre: the fishing spot marker (table pond, radius 22 m) stands at the pond centre on the bed, and the rest is on the east bank, whose shore line runs north-south at x about 4690.7. A vanilla wooden pier (Pier_Wood_Long_01, 9.2 m, long axis east-west) is the jetty: its east end rests on the bank and its deck is 0.3 m above the water (mount free, y 2.75 under the barn's ground). A street bench on the bank south of the jetty faces the water, and a pole plate sign (id spring-pond) stands north of the jetty facing the road. Rows are rigid: shift, never stretch."
